    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n72705" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἴφω</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		=<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀχεύω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1
				</span></i>
			, but only of human beings, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰν Χελιδονίδα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Pyrrh.</u>
					28
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(3).536
			</span></i> (Thera, <span class="entity">vii B. C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Leg.Gort.</u>
				2.3
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰφεῖ,</span> as if from
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰφέω,</span> in prov. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄριστα χωλὸς οἰ.,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Mimn.
				15
			</span></i> Diehl, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Com.Adesp.</u>
				36
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Diogenian.
				2.2
			</span></i> :—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰφόλης</span></b> , and fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰφόλις</span></b> , <i>lewd,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				12(5).97
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Naxos</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1597.29
			</span></i>.</div>
